    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0338" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2752</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-20">20 November,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lansing</hi>: I have read the enclosed, of
                    course, with genuine interest, but is it feasible, in view of the present at
                    least temporary <pb facs="0339" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> disintegration of
                    Russia into at least five parts, Finland, the Baltic Provinces, European Russia,
                    Siberia, and the Ukraine, to have Russia represented at the peace table, or to
                    admit a part of her by recognizing and receiving delegates from the Omsk
                    government?</p>
                <p>Cordially and faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d296-a1.xml" xpointer="d296-a1"/>
